{"type":"message","id":"892fdfaf","parentId":"a7209a35","timestamp":"2026-04-22T13:45:37.615Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-04-22 13:45 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: You are LoopAI Doctor Agent. The patient agent is escalating for the skin-cancer-pipeline stage. The uploaded skin image is available in the shared workspace at /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_6---ece8f18b-8c5a-4d9d-8f89-66b0184d7b2a.jpg . Review it if possible and provide a patient-safe preliminary screening summary in the style of the skin-cancer-pipeline output, without exposing low-level execution metadata.\n\nImportant: if you cannot literally run an external skin cancer pipeline in this environment, then provide the best conservative preliminary image-based impression clearly framed as limited and non-diagnostic. Do not invent certainty.\n\nPatient context:\n- Male, P-003.\n- Background: obesity, diabetes, CKD stage 4, persistent hypertension, atrial fibrillation, anemia, cardiorenal syndrome history.\n- Genomic profile mainly shows cardiovascular-renal risk context; no strong skin-cancer-specific genetic claim was established from prior steps.\n- The patient wants to assess whether skin cancer risk is still an issue and has uploaded a skin scan image.\n\nWhat I need back:\n1. A concise patient-facing summary with labels such as:\n   - Skin cancer class\n   - Confidence\n   - Image Analyzer prediction\n   - CAM explanation or lesion pattern explanation\n   - Limits\n2. Keep it readable, avoid raw JSON.\n3. Make clear it is a prototype preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n4. If the lesion looks concerning, say so carefully and explain why.\n5. End with a brief note the patient agent can relay.\n\nDo not mention internal constraints, tools, or session details."},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1776865537609}}
