utward**, and **somewhat irregular borders/pigment distribution**. That pattern is **not fully reassuring** on visual review.  \n- **CAM / lesion pattern explanation:** The visually important areas are the **dark central pigment**, the **uneven spread of color**, and the **blurred or irregular outer edge**. In plain terms, the spot does not look uniformly round or evenly colored, which is why it deserves caution.  \n- **Limits:** A photo alone cannot confirm cancer type or whether this is melanoma, another pigmented lesion, or a benign atypical mole. Image quality, lighting, magnification, and lack of size/history all limit confidence. Clinical exam and often dermoscopy, sometimes biopsy, are needed.\n\n**Bottom line:**  \nThis image shows a **preliminary concerning signal**, mainly because of **asymmetry and irregular pigmentation**, so I would **not treat it as clearly benign** from the image alone.\n\n**Brief note to relay:**  \n“This is a prototype, non-diagnostic screening result. Because the lesion looks somewhat irregular and unevenly pigmented, it would be reasonable to arrange an in-person dermatology review, especially if it is new, changing, bleeding, itching, or enlarging.”","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e50ad4bdb9e1d3c0169e8d1044a70819186ee067bddae1a2d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":7126,"output":392,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7518,"cost":{"input":0.017815,"output":0.00588,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.023695}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776865537616,"responseId":"resp_0e50ad4bdb9e1d3c0169e8d101e55c8191b8a66edb1e2f2c50"}}
